Helios DXVK fork: direct image mapping on NVK on RM (opt-in)

Conduit guest/windows. Applied after 0022 by ci/windows/Build-Driver.ps1;
it does not depend on 0023.

The fork defaults d3d11.disableDirectImageMapping to true for every device.
The reason is Venus-only. A direct-mapped image is LINEAR, host-visible and
PREINITIALIZED, so it cannot carry VkExternalMemoryImageCreateInfo. vkr
exports all host-visible memory anyway, the host NVIDIA driver drops the
bind, and the GPU reads zeros. On NVK on RM (HELIOS_DXVK_BACKEND=nvk) there
is no vkr. NVK makes external memory only for shared images. Direct mapping
is used only for D3D11_USAGE_DYNAMIC textures: one mip and one layer, LINEAR
supported, and one row, video-shaped or larger than 1 MiB.

With the option on, every such texture goes through DXVK's DYNAMIC path:
- Map(WRITE_DISCARD) gets a staging buffer.
- Unmap records a buffer-to-image copy on the CS thread.
- The copy runs outside a render pass, so an Unmap between draws ends the
  render pass.
- The GPU copies the data a second time.

HELIOS_DXVK_DIRECT_IMAGE_MAPPING=1 gives an NVK device DXVK's upstream
default, so direct mapping is allowed. A Venus device keeps the option on.
d3d11.disableDirectImageMapping in a DXVK config, DXVK_CONFIG or an app
profile still wins. The first device that has the knob logs one line.

Default off: direct-mapped textures on NVK on RM have not been checked under
the installed driver yet.

diff --git a/src/d3d11/d3d11_options.cpp b/src/d3d11/d3d11_options.cpp
index bf102080..bbb984c2 100644
--- a/src/d3d11/d3d11_options.cpp
+++ b/src/d3d11/d3d11_options.cpp
@@ -1,3 +1,6 @@
+#include <atomic>
+
+#include "../dxvk/dxvk_helios_backend.h"
 #include "../util/util_math.h"
 
 #include "d3d11_options.h"
@@ -40,7 +43,30 @@ namespace dxvk {
     // dwm's black wallpaper / solid-color / mica brush surfaces. Force every
     // mappable image through the buffer-backed paths (which carry the
     // matching handleTypes fix in vn_buffer.c).
-    this->disableDirectImageMapping = config.getOption<bool>("d3d11.disableDirectImageMapping", true);
+    //
+    // Conduit: none of that exists on NVK on RM (HELIOS_DXVK_BACKEND=nvk):
+    // NVK makes no external memory unless DXVK asks for a shared image, and
+    // only D3D11_USAGE_DYNAMIC textures are mapped directly. With
+    // HELIOS_DXVK_DIRECT_IMAGE_MAPPING=1 an NVK device gets DXVK's own
+    // default (direct mapping allowed); a Venus device keeps it disabled.
+    // d3d11.disableDirectImageMapping in a DXVK config or app profile still
+    // wins.
+    static const bool s_heliosDirectImageMapping =
+      env::getEnvVar("HELIOS_DXVK_DIRECT_IMAGE_MAPPING") == "1";
+
+    const bool heliosDirectMap = s_heliosDirectImageMapping && heliosBackendNvk();
+
+    this->disableDirectImageMapping = config.getOption<bool>("d3d11.disableDirectImageMapping", !heliosDirectMap);
+
+    if (heliosDirectMap) {
+      static std::atomic<bool> s_heliosDirectMapLogged = { false };
+
+      if (!s_heliosDirectMapLogged.exchange(true)) {
+        Logger::info(str::format("Helios: NVK direct image mapping ",
+          this->disableDirectImageMapping ? "disabled by d3d11.disableDirectImageMapping"
+                                          : "allowed (HELIOS_DXVK_DIRECT_IMAGE_MAPPING=1)"));
+      }
+    }
 
     // Clamp LOD bias so that people don't abuse this in unintended ways
     this->samplerLodBias = dxvk::fclamp(this->samplerLodBias, -2.0f, 1.0f);
